.TH clerestory 1  "clerestory 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
clerestory \- Hardware\-Adaptive Windows 11 KVM Optimizer & Provisioning Engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBclerestory\fR [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clerestory inspects Linux host silicon topology (L3 cache/CCD boundaries, SMT thread pairs, NUMA, hugepages) and synthesizes near\-bare\-metal Windows 11 KVM virtual machines with automated driver slipstreaming.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential terminal output and progress spinners
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase logging verbosity (\-v for INFO, \-vv for DEBUG, \-vvv for TRACE)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable ANSI color output
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
clerestory\-doctor(1)
Interrogate host silicon hardware, kernel flags, and virtualization prerequisites
.TP
clerestory\-create(1)
Provision a new hardware\-optimized Windows 11 VM
.TP
clerestory\-inspect(1)
Inspect a provisioned VM configuration and topology mapping
.TP
clerestory\-list(1)
List all managed Windows 11 VMs and their runtime state
.TP
clerestory\-start(1)
Start a provisioned Windows 11 VM
.TP
clerestory\-stop(1)
Gracefully stop a running Windows 11 VM
.TP
clerestory\-destroy(1)
Undefine and clean up a Windows 11 VM
.TP
clerestory\-completions(1)
Generate shell auto\-completion scripts
.TP
clerestory\-man(1)
Generate ROFF man pages for distribution
.TP
clerestory\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
